WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.000
FastAPI.

2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:09.198
It's the default chassis for LLM services, so most example code you'll read from here on simply assumes it.

3
00:00:09.198 --> 00:00:10.100
Let's see why.

4
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:15.767
FastAPI is the modern Python framework for building APIs.

5
00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:21.000
Under the hood it's an ASGI app, built on Starlette and served by uvicorn.

6
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:27.567
That makes it async native, which matters when every request spends seconds waiting on an LLM provider.

7
00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:30.633
Here's the stack, from the bottom up.

8
00:00:30.933 --> 00:00:33.800
Uvicorn is the server that listens for requests.

9
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.833
Starlette gives it async plumbing.

10
00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:39.167
FastAPI adds the type-hint magic on top.

11
00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:42.300
And your routes sit at the very top, small and clean.

12
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.733
The same annotations do three jobs.

13
00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:52.733
First, you declare the request shape, and FastAPI rejects bad input with a precise four twenty two error.

14
00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:56.080
Second, the response model is your output contract.

15
00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:57.633
Extra fields are stripped.

16
00:00:57.933 --> 00:01:03.233
Third, a live docs page appears at slash docs, generated from the very same hints.

17
00:01:04.433 --> 00:01:05.900
Here's a real endpoint.

18
00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:11.633
One class describes what a request must contain: a question, and an optional top k.

19
00:01:11.933 --> 00:01:15.400
Another describes the response: an answer and its sources.

20
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.867
The route is async, and it declares that response model.

21
00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:24.400
Inside, we await retrieval, await the model, and return the answer with source ids.

22
00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:26.867
Now the real payoff.

23
00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:29.733
Your RAG has lived in notebooks for a long time.

24
00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:36.967
This endpoint becomes its public face: a question about mission logs goes in, an answer with sources comes out.

25
00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:40.367
When a teammate asks how to call it, you don't write docs.

26
00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:43.467
You send the docs link, and they test it from the browser.

27
00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:45.647
Let's recap.

28
00:01:45.647 --> 00:01:49.567
FastAPI is the default chassis for LLM services.

29
00:01:49.867 --> 00:01:53.967
Your type hints validate input, shape output, and generate docs.

30
00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:56.367
It's ASGI and async native.

31
00:01:56.667 --> 00:02:00.044
So share the docs link instead of writing a manual.

32
00:02:00.044 --> 00:02:01.700
Next up: Pydantic models.
